{'symbol': 'BA', 'date': '2020-01-11 19:30:00', 'title': 'Boeing - Dennis Muilenburg Is Not Entitled To Any Severance Or Separation Payments In Connection With His Retirement', 'text': "BOEING - DENNIS MUILENBURG IS NOT ENTITLED TO-AND DID NOT RECEIVE-ANY SEVERANCE OR SEPARATION PAYMENTS IN CONNECTION WITH HIS RETIREMENT.BOEING - ON JANUARY 10, 2020, BOARD APPROVED COMPENSATION FOR DAVID L. CALHOUN IN CONNECTION WITH HIS NEW ROLE.BOEING - CALHOUN WILL RECEIVE A BASE SALARY AT AN ANNUAL RATE OF $1.4 MILLION.BOEING - MUILENBURG WILL RECEIVE NO PAYMENT UNDER COMPANY’S ANNUAL INCENTIVE PLAN FOR 2019.BOEING - MUILENBURG IS ENTITLED TO CONTRACTUAL, PRE-EXISTING RETIREMENT BENEFITS.BOEING - MUILENBURG FORFEITED 11,266 RSUS, 10,398 PERFORMANCE-BASED RESTRICTED STOCK UNITS, 72,746 PERFORMANCE AWARDS IN CONNECTION WITH RETIREMENT.BOEING - CALHOUN'S INCENTIVE AWARDS WILL BE SUBJECT TO AN ENHANCED CLAWBACK POLICY.BOEING - BASED ON CLOSING STOCK PRICE ON JANUARY 9, MUILENBURG'S FORFEITED AWARDS WOULD HAVE BEEN VALUED AT ABOUT $14.6 MILLION.BOEING - BASED ON CLOSING STOCK PRICE ON JANUARY 9, MUILENBURG'S VESTED LONG-TERM INCENTIVE AWARDS WOULD BE VALUED AT ABOUT $29.4 MILLION.BOEING - MUILENBURG WILL RECEIVE DISTRIBUTIONS OF PENSION, NONQUALIFIED DEFERRED COMPENSATION BENEFITS EARNED DURING HIS TENURE.BOEING - BOARD APPROVED PAYMENT OF AN ANNUAL CASH RETAINER OF $250,000 TO LAWRENCE W, KELLNER, COMPANY'S NON-EXECUTIVE BOARD CHAIRMAN.BOEING - KEVIN MCALLISTER FORFEITED 100,000 UNVESTED RSUS THAT WERE AWARDED IN CONNECTION WITH HIS HIRE IN 2016."}
